# Module Isolation Compliance (always binding)

Every change must respect `docs/01-architecture/module-isolation-rules.md`.
Violations cause silent breaks, seal bypasses, and CI gaps.

## Before editing

1. Read `docs/01-architecture/module-isolation-rules.md` (full contract).
2. If the change touches a sealed `@asol/*` package, read that package's section in the same doc.
3. Identify which declared door(s) the call site may use — never reach internals.

## The eight rules (summary)

| # | Rule |
|---|------|
| 1 | Sensitive logic stays inside the core module |
| 2 | Interact only through declared public API doors |
| 3 | Unit + integration tests must gate the build |
| 4 | Modules validate their own inputs at boundaries |
| 5 | No deep imports of internal files |
| 6 | Branch protection + required CI checks stay green |
| 7 | Packages are independent (`packages/<name>`) |
| 8 | Single responsibility per file |
| 9 | Dependency upgrades stay inside the owning module |

## Forbidden patterns

- Deep imports: `@asol/<pkg>/src/...`, `@asol/<pkg>/internal/...`, or any path not in `exports`
- Relative imports into `packages/` from `src/` (e.g. `../packages/foo/src/index`)
- Wildcard `exports` (`"./*"`) or `tsconfig` `"@asol/<name>/*"` path aliases
- Wiring app code directly to another package's internals instead of its door
- Adding a new public surface without updating `package.json` `exports` and contract tests

## Package boundaries

- Import only through doors listed in each package's `package.json` `exports` map.
- Browser vs server: use the correct door (e.g. `@asol/storage-core` vs `@asol/storage-core/server`).
- Composition packages (`*-composition`) wire ports; capability packages (`*-core`) own logic.
- When unsure which door to use, search the doc section for that package before coding.

## CI gates (must stay green)

```text
npm run architecture:check
```

Run the relevant `test:*-core` or `test:compositions` script for any package you touch.
Any change that breaks these gates is incomplete.

## Docs

When a change affects package doors, boundaries, or enforcement, update
`docs/01-architecture/module-isolation-rules.md` in the same change (English only).
